{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"2a35a73fad2add38d6333e6c405778dba6b20f953958512e1ba0a663690b5cba","packTokens":1825,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":162,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1054,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":503,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write its sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true, so no test may count on those rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"The web app is built in its own repo; do not build screens here.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"The product stories describe behaviors beyond the locked API contract, while the final instruction says to implement the contract exactly. When a story requires behavior the contract does not define, which scope should govern?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Implement only operations and behavior defined by the locked OpenAPI contract; do not add uncontracted behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"For sample rows that refer to one another, should the seeder create compatible references, or may it seed each table independently?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Create compatible references between related sample rows.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"The contract includes an operation to return a configured staff identity-provider authorization URL, but the provider and source of that configuration are not identified here. What should the API use?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the existing staff identity provider and supply its authorization URL and token-validation settings through deployment configuration.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"When demo seeding is disabled and a database table has no records, should list operations return an empty list or provide sample rows without persisting them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Return an empty list when the database has no matching records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"The staff identity-provider URL and token-validation settings will come from deployment configuration. What should happen if required settings are missing or invalid?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail application startup with a clear configuration error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"How should schema changes be applied to databases that already exist when the new persistent tables are introduced?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply a reviewed database migration during deployment, preserving existing data; use EnsureCreated only for genuinely empty databases.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"With demo seeding disabled, how should the first PostgreSQL account be made available so the API can authorize callers?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Have deployment provision the initial account outside the API; do not add an API bootstrap flow.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"Which staff identity provider and concrete authorization-URL and token-validation settings should the API use?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Identify the organization's existing staff provider and supply its authorization URL and validation settings; do not introduce a new provider.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the test and factory runs obtain the valid nonproduction identity-provider settings required for startup?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Provide valid nonproduction settings for the chosen provider through test and factory configuration.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"How much customer-authentication behavior beyond the locked contract should be specified for failed logins and password storage?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep behavior limited to the locked contract; use standard secure password hashing for stored passwords, and do not add new lockout or one-time-code policies.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"Which token claim should identify the PostgreSQL staff account, and what should happen if a valid token has no matching or has a disabled account?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Match the token's email claim to the account email, and deny access when no matching enabled account exists.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement only the operations and behavior defined in the OpenAPI contract, retaining the root health, OpenAPI-document, and Swagger UI routes, and ensure responses, filtering, and scope enforcement conform to the contract.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Persist contract-defined business changes in the configured PostgreSQL database, apply only contract-defined lifecycle constraints, use EnsureCreated only for a genuinely empty database, and use a reviewed migration that preserves existing data for existing databases.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Run the demo seeder at startup only when Seed:Demo is true; have it add two to five contract-example-based rows only to each empty contract-backed table, preserve existing rows, and create valid references.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"When demo seeding is false or unset, do not run the seeder or create demo rows, and return empty lists for collection operations with no matching persisted records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Use the organization’s existing staff identity provider, with authorization URL and token-validation settings from deployment configuration and valid nonproduction settings in test and factory runs; fail startup with an error identifying any missing or invalid required setting.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer and staff authentication and authorization only through the contract; store customer passwords as salted hashes, authorize using PostgreSQL account roles and scopes, match staff token email claims to enabled account emails, deny unmatched or disabled accounts, and add no extra lockout or one-time-code policies.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Provision the initial PostgreSQL account through deployment, outside the API.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}